Legal Team, CTO, Compliance, CEO:

Volkswagen AG has identified a software defect in the
gateway software supplied by your company for VW ID.7
and ID. Buzz platforms. A formal recall has been initiated.

Recall Details:
  VW Recall Number: 9148-B2-2026
  Component: Central Gateway Module (CGM) software
  Platform: MEB (ID.7, ID. Buzz, ID.4, ID.5)
  Affected Vehicles: 184,224 worldwide
  Software Version: v2.3.1 - v2.4.7
  Defect: Email filtering failure in connected services
  Risk: HIGH — Credential theft in connected services
  Initiated: October 28, 2026
  KBA Notified: October 30, 2026

Supplier Response Process:

  1. VW will send a formal recall notification letter
     by REGISTERED MAIL to your legal department

  2. You have 60 days to respond with:
     - Root cause analysis (8D report)
     - Corrective action plan
     - Software fix timeline

  3. Cost sharing is negotiated between VW Procurement
     and your sales team — NOT paid through email bank
     transfers

  4. FRSU compliance documentation is submitted through
     your VW Procurement contact (same channel as your
     normal supplier communications)

  Important Security Notes:
  VW will NEVER:
  - Send bank details for "supplier contribution" via email
  - Create "CARIAD Software Services GmbH" for supplier
    recall payments
  - Require source code submission through email portals
  - Ask for ECU firmware through online links
  - Offer a "Chinese supplier channel"
  - Set a "November 30 deadline" for €2.2M payment

  VW's actual recall process:
  - Formal notification by registered mail
  - Technical response through your VW Procurement
    contact (email or phone — but never with bank
    details or source code requests)
  - Source code is shared only under NDA through
    VW's secure development infrastructure, not
    through email portals
  - Cost sharing is negotiated, not demanded via
    email with bank details
  - You have 60 days (not 27 days)

  If you receive an email requesting €2.2M payment
  to a "CARIAD" entity or asking for ECU source code
  upload through a portal link, it is a phishing
  attempt targeting automotive suppliers.

Your Rights:
  60 days to respond (not 27 days)
  Cost sharing is negotiable, not unilateral
  Source code shared under NDA through secure channels

